# Wave W17-M (Route 108): wreck rock — the rib-reef: four curved hull ribs standing out of the water in warm wreck timbers, the lane filing past between them, foam collar where the surf combs through, the sea baked in around it (design: a broken hull with exposed ribs standing in the foam mid-lane; no shipped hull kind exists — the rock conversion carries her). Route 108’s own rock — ribs, not stone: no other lane’s rock is drawn in curves.
